== Modernization & Sustainability
- Among the *top 25* in the world for sustainable development.
#pause
- Goal: *zero carbon dioxide emissions by 2035*.
#pause
- The business school is moving to a new modern complex in the city center.
#pause
- Scientific laboratories are expanding; digital technologies are being introduced into education.
#pause
- Support programs make quality education accessible to talented children from different social backgrounds.

== Internationality
- Students and staff from *more than 130 countries*.
#pause
- Among the top 50 most international universities in the world (Times Higher Education).
#pause
- Exchange trips, internships and summer schools in Europe, Asia, America and Africa.
#pause
- *Support for newcomers:* free meeting at Newcastle airport, a special study week, visa advice and academic English help.

= Traditions and Student Life

== College Life
- Each college has an *elected student council* that independently organizes holidays, clubs and volunteer projects.
#pause
- *Formal dinners:* the main hallmark of Durham; students at the oldest colleges wear traditional academic robes.
#pause
- *Themed parties, annual summer balls* and *college days* are held throughout the year.
