= Quiz Time

== Question 1 (History)
*Who initiated the founding of Durham University in 1832?*
#pause

- A) King William IV
- B) Bishop William van Mildert
- C) Robert Swan
- D) Guillaume V

#pause
*Answer: B) Bishop William van Mildert*

== Question 2 (Structure)
*How many colleges are there at Durham University?*
#pause

- A) 12
- B) 17
- C) 27
- D) 300

#pause
*Answer: B) 17*

== Question 3 (Traditions)
*What is the main hallmark of student life at Durham, for which students wear traditional academic robes?*
#pause

- A) Formal dinners
- B) Summer balls
- C) Team Durham matches
- D) Scientific picnic

#pause
*Answer: A) Formal dinners*

== Question 4 (Alumni)
*Which Durham alumnus became the first person in history to walk to both poles of the Earth?*
#pause

- A) Nasser Hussain
- B) Sir Harold Evans
- C) Robert Swan
- D) Carlos Frenk

#pause
*Answer: C) Robert Swan*

== Question 5 (Development)
*By which year does Durham aim to reach zero carbon dioxide emissions?*
#pause

- A) 2030
- B) 2035
- C) 2040
- D) 2050

#pause
*Answer: B) 2035*

